   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T34"><text:span text:style-name="T34">You can add App Store Connect users (normally users in your organization) to test the app. There is a link at the left for </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T38">Add External Testers</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34">. This will require the app to go through Beta App Review.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc74121625"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354471"/>Apple Privacy Policy<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc74121625"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354471"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T34"><text:span text:style-name="T34">Prior to publishing your app through </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T38">App Store Connect</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34">, you will be required to complete the privacy policy details section. <text:s/>The answers to these questions will be used to create the privacy policy section in your app store entry that describes to the user how you are using their data. <text:s/>The types of data associated with each question is documented by Apple at </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://developer.apple.com/app-store/app-privacy-details/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T34">https://developer.apple.com/app-store/app-privacy-details/</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T34">. <text:s/>The answers associated with the SAB app depend upon the use of analytics and what data is saved if you have user registration defined for your app. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P61" text:outline-level="2" loext:marker-style-name="T30"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc74121626"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354472"/><text:span text:style-name="T30">Data Types</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc74121626"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354472"/><text:span text:style-name="T30"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T34"><text:span text:style-name="T34">Under the initial </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Data Collection</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> screen in this section, if the app does not use analytics or user registration, you may indicate that the app does not collect any data. <text:s/>If either of these features are in use, then you should respond that we do collect data from this app. <text:s/>If you answer </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Yes</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> to this question, then you need to specify in the next screen the types of data collected. <text:s/>For an app that has analytics enabled, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Product Interaction</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> under </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Usage Data</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Crash Data </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34">under </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Diagnostics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> should be selected. <text:s/>If the app has User Registration enabled, then some of the fields under </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Contact Info</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> may need to be checked depending upon the fields you have configured for the user to enter.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P61" text:outline-level="2" loext:marker-style-name="T30"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc74121627"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354473"/><text:span text:style-name="T30">Product Interaction</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc74121627"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354473"/><text:span text:style-name="T30"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T44"><text:span text:style-name="T34">This section should only be required if analytics or user registration are enabled. <text:s/>If analytics is enabled, then the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">Analytics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> entry should be checked to indicate that the data is being used to track user behavior. <text:s/>If user registration is enabled, you may also want to check the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">App Functionality</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34"> entry. On the next screen, you should check the “</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">No, product interaction data collected from this app is not linked to the user’s identity</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T34">” entry. On the final screen, regarding tracking, you may click the “</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">No, we do not product interaction data for tracking purposes”.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15" loext:marker-style-name="T11"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354474"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="OLE_LINK1"/>Building from Terminal<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354474"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc475369926"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T2">Reading App Builder has a command line interface which allows you to create a new app and build it or load an existing app and build it. <text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2"/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P61" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228353930"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354475"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354156"/>Installing Command Line Interface<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228353930"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354475"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354156"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T74"><text:span text:style-name="T52">Choose the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T48">Tools</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T48">Install rab command in PATH</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T74">menu item to enable the use of the command line interface. <text:s/>You will be prompted to enter your login password to install the command.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P61" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228353931"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354476"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354157"/>Command Line Interface Options<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228353931"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354476"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354157"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T2">Run the following command to run the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">Reading</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2"> App Builder application followed by a series of options described below. <text:s/>The command is:</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T52">r</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2">ab</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T2"><text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P52" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T2">The available parameters are:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T2"><text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2"/></text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table3" table:style-name="Table3">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table3.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table3.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P71" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T18">Option</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T18"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P71" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T18">Description</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T18"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-new</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Create a new app project</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-load &lt;project&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Load an existing app project</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-build</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Build app project (use with either -new or -load)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-no-save</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Do not save changes to app (use with -load)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-resign</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Resign iOS Template App (use with either -new or -load)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-?</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Show command line help</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-n &lt;app-name&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set app name.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Enclose the name in &quot;double quotes&quot; if it contains spaces.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-p &lt;package-name&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set package name, e.g. com.myorg.language.appname</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-b &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Add book or bundle file. This could be a USFM file or a zipped set of USFM files. It could also be a Digital Bible Library text release bundle.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-i &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Include additional parameters file.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Use the full path of the file and enclose it in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-a &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set about box text, contained in text file.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Use the full path of the file and enclose it in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-f &lt;fontname&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set font name or filename, e.g. &quot;Charis SIL Compact&quot;, &quot;c:\fonts\myfont.ttf&quot;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">The font name must be one of the items in the list of fonts in the New App wizard. For other fonts, specify the full path to the font filename.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-g</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Use Grandroid</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-ic &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Add launcher icon (one or more .png files).</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Use the full path of the files and enclose them in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-l &lt;lang-code&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set language for menu items and settings, e.g. en, fr, es</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-ft &lt;feature=value&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set a feature, e.g. book-select=grid</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-vc &lt;integer&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set version code, e.g. 1, 2, 3, or +1 to increment the current version code by 1.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-vn &lt;string&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set version name, e.g. 1.0, 2.1.4, or use +1, +0.1, +0.0.1 to increment the current value.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-ks &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set keystore filename.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Use the full path of the file and enclose it in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-ksp &lt;password&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set keystore password</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-ka &lt;alias&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set key alias</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-kap &lt;password&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set key alias password</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-fp &lt;folder=path&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set a folder path, e.g. &quot;app.builder=/Developer/Reading App Builder&quot;.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-ta &lt;target-api&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set Target API, e.g. 21 for Android 5.0, 22 for Android 5.1.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P118" loext:marker-style-name="T68"/>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P21" loext:marker-style-name="T4"/>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-si &lt;signing identity&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set Signing Identity to use for iOS Resigning</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-pp &lt;provisioning profile&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set full path to provisioning profile for iOS resigning</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-bn &lt;integer&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set build number for ipa file, e.g. 1, 2, 3, or +1 to increment by 1</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T68"><text:span text:style-name="T69">-vs &lt;string&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T69"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P68" loext:marker-style-name="T4"><text:span text:style-name="T4">Set version string for ipa file, e.g. 1.0, 2.1.4 or +1, +0.1, +0.0.1</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T1"><text:span text:style-name="T83"><text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T83"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T1"><text:span text:style-name="T17">Examples:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T17"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T70">rab -load &quot;Mali&quot; -resign -bn &quot;5&quot; -vs &quot;2.3.2&quot; -si &quot;iPhone Distribution: Summer Institute of Linguistics, Inc (SIL) (4YF5X97M4H) &quot; -pp &quot;/Users/builder/Documents/MobileProvision/AdHoc_org.wycliffe.app.mali.mobileprovision&quot;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2"> </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P50" loext:marker-style-name="T2"><text:span text:style-name="T2">Running the command line with no parameters will start the Reading App Builder UI from the command line.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2"/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P220" text:outline-level="1" loext:marker-style-name="T26"><text:bookmark-end text:name="OLE_LINK1"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354477"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc73705825"/><text:span text:style-name="T26">Using Firebase in an iOS App</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354477"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc73705825"/><text:span text:style-name="T26"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T84"><text:span text:style-name="T19">The </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20">Building Apps</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T19"> document contains general information </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T84">about setting up the app to support Firebase Analytics, Crashlytics, Messaging and Real Time Database. <text:s/>This section will focus on the steps required to make these features work with an iOS app.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P221" text:outline-level="2" loext:marker-style-name="T27"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc73705826"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354478"/><text:span text:style-name="T27">Adding an iOS App</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc73705826"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354478"/><text:span text:style-name="T27"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T51"><text:span text:style-name="T51">The first step is to go to your Firebase Console (</text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://console.firebase.google.com/u/0/" text:style-name="ListLabel_20_404" text:visited-style-name="ListLabel_20_404"><text:span text:style-name="T85">https://console.firebase.google.com/u/0/</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T51">) <text:s/>and select the entry for the application you are working on. <text:s/>Press the “Add App” button, then select the iOS button.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T1"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="Picture 478048538" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="5in" svg:height="2.5626in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
