   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T74"><text:span text:style-name="T74">After making these changes, the provisioning profile for the app should be updated for the new capability and the entry updated in SAB.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T74"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P111" loext:marker-style-name="T74"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T74"><text:span text:style-name="T74">For Firebase to send notification to the app, it will need to have a key uploaded to it. <text:s/>The preferred manner is to go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T76">Keys </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T74">section in Apple Developer and select to create an Apple Push Notifications service key, using the first option on the screen below. <text:s/>One key of this type is created to be used with all apps associated with this organization. <text:s/>If a key has already been created, then use that. <text:s/></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T74"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="Picture 31" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="6.2638in" svg:height="4.1354in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
